    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Note: per-pod NFS attribution",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "VictoriaMetrics"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 44,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**cAdvisor per-pod network metrics do NOT capture NFS traffic.** The pod sees writes to `/downloads` etc. as filesystem syscalls (bind-mounted), not as packets through its veth. The actual NFS RPCs happen at the kubelet level and show up as host traffic on the worker's `ens19` interface (top of this dashboard). For per-pod NFS attribution we'd need a TrueNAS-side exporter or eBPF agent \u2014 neither is currently deployed. CPU+memory of media pods (above) is the best in-cluster proxy for 'who's busy doing NFS work right now'."
      }
    }
